course: dictionary
lesson: 14832
title: Racer
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A racer is someone or something that takes part in a race. The word comes from race, and the -er ending shows a person or thing that does the action. «The racer crossed the finish line first.» Here a racer is a competitor, a person who runs, rides or drives to win.
explain: Racer can also name a machine built for speed. «She rode her new racer bike to the park.» A racer bike is made for racing, so it is light and fast. A «go-kart racer» is a person who races a small kart, and the same clue tells you what the word means.
explain: Check the clues around the word. If the sentence talks about a track, a start line or a finish, racer means a competitor. If it talks about a bike, car or boat, it may mean a machine built for racing. Test your meaning by swapping in «competitor» or «fast machine» and checking that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can also name animals. In the US, a racer is a kind of fast snake, such as the black racer. The spelling stays the same in every case, so the clues in the sentence decide which meaning is right.
fact: A racer is a person, animal or machine that takes part in races.
fact: A «racer bike» is a bike built for racing, not for everyday riding.
fact: A «go-kart racer» is a person who races a small kart.
fact: In the US, a racer can also be a kind of fast snake, such as the black racer.
fact: Racer is a noun, and its plural is racers.
exercise: «The racer crossed the finish line first.» What is the racer in this sentence? | A road sign | A referee who starts the race | A spectator in the stands | *A competitor who takes part in the race
exercise: «She rode her new racer bike to the park.» What kind of bike is a racer bike? | *A bike built for racing | A bike made of wood | A bike with a basket for shopping | A folding bike for the train
exercise: Which word is the plural of racer? | race | *racers | racerish | racerer
test: «The go-kart racer waved to the crowd.» What does racer mean here? | A type of cake | *A person who takes part in the race | A bus driver | A teacher who waves
test: In the US, what can racer also mean? | A kind of cloud | *A kind of fast snake | A kind of bread | A kind of bell
exam: «The cycle racer pedalled hard up the hill.» What does racer mean in this sentence? | A hill walker | A bike shop worker | A person who fixes bikes | *A cyclist taking part in a race
